    {
      "id": "4c363eb2-68e4-4d04-a82f-92b8a0b6fc6f",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 624,
        "height": 688,
        "content": "### How it works\n\nCompanies in Japan that operate vehicles for business must test every\ndriver for alcohol before and after each shift, and keep the records\nfor a year. Missing even one entry is a compliance failure, so someone\nchecks the list by hand every evening.\n\nThis workflow has two entry points on purpose. Drivers submit their\nresult through a form at any time, and a scheduled run in the evening\ncompares the day's submissions against who was rostered. Anyone with\nno record gets a polite reminder, the manager gets a one-line summary,\nand the gap is logged.\n\nThe match key combines driver, date and shift, so a driver who tested\nbefore the shift but not after is still caught. The workflow only\ndetects missing records — it never judges the measured value and never\nimplies wrongdoing.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n1. Add your Google Sheets, Gemini, Gmail and Slack credentials.\n2. Copy the sample spreadsheet, then paste its ID into \"Configure check\n   rules\" and \"Save test record\". Set the roster dates to today so the\n   first run has something to find. Keep the header rows unchanged, as\n   the Sheets nodes map fields by column name.\n3. Set the workflow timezone to your local zone, since the match key\n   is built from the submission date.\n4. Share the form URL with your drivers.\n5. Run once manually, then activate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ef6fbe18-7455-4ac1-bd17-e1aedc76bf2e",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        816
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FFFFFF",
        "width": 1360,
        "height": 256,
        "content": "Collect test records\nDrivers submit through the form at any time. The date is added here\nrather than asked for, so a mistyped date can never break the match.\nThe confirming staff member is recorded, as the check must be\nwitnessed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c6a89387-b83e-4f89-be39-698b19acf978",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        1184
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FFFFFF",
        "width": 1376,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "Compare roster with records\nThe roster and the submitted records are merged on the match key.\nKeep Non-Matches from input 1 is used on purpose: this workflow looks\nfor what is absent, not what is present. Only rows dated today are\nconsidered, so update the sample roster before your first run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "09a244be-a68a-4562-96e8-8214cd82d227",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        1664
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FFFFFF",
        "width": 1520,
        "height": 368,
        "content": "Decide who to chase\nThe results are collapsed into a single item so the next step runs\neven when nothing is missing. The LLM step retries on failure, since\na transient API error would otherwise skip a whole day's check."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "64fa88e2-a5dc-453a-a685-28df19f05f85",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        2064
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FFFFFF",
        "width": 1956,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "Notify and log\nBoth branches reach Slack, so the manager hears from the workflow every\nevening whether or not anything was missed. The gaps are shaped into log\nrows and appended, which is what the annual record requirement needs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
